or Peyton Reed has to say  about this movie and Kang the Conqueror  and you're truly going to realize that  Kang is truly a force to be reckoned  with and this movie is going to be huge  in an interview with Entertainment  Weekly he expressed that the previous  Ant-Man films were seen AS Palette  cleansers and he wanted to change that  so in the interview he said people felt  like oh these are fun little palette  cleansers after a gigantic Avengers  movie for this third one I said I don't  want to be the palette cleanser anymore  I want to be the big Avengers movie when  telling him this I metaphorically kicked  in Kevin feige's door and here's where  he gives us some details about what to  expect from Kang the Conqueror in the  film he continues in the interview I  grew up a real Marvel Comics nerd and  there are a handful of antagonists in  the Marvel Comics universe who are  Alzheimer's Loki obviously Dr Doom from  the Fantastic Four and Kang the Kong  conqueror in conversations with Kevin  feige and Marvel it was like I want to  put Ant-Man and wasp up against a really  formidable villain in this movie and so  we're doing King the Conqueror in the  comics King has dominion over time he's  a time traveler his situation is a  little bit different in this movie which  I won't spoil for you but he's someone  while we live very linear lives from  childhood to death Kang doesn't exist  that way it struck me as interesting to  take the tiniest Avengers in some  people's mind maybe the least powerful  Avengers and put them up against the  most powerful force in the Multiverse  now I love that final line where he says  Kang the Conqueror is the most powerful  force in the Multiverse this is why he  is going to be the big bat however we  already know that we are going to see  more than one Kang variant in  quantumania we so far know about at  least two and one of them is going to be  asking Ant-Man for his help to take down  the other because remember the true  multiversal war that happened before in  the past was between a bunch of  different variants of Kang it wasn't a  bunch of Avengers fighting each other it  was literally just variants of King and  in this Comet that he makes where he  says he's not going to spoil the movie  This is actually what he is referring to  he is referring to one of the variants  of Kang that we're going to be  introduced to in Quantum Mania you see  in this interview what he said although  he doesn't reveal it because of course  spoilers he is actually talking about  two kings one of them is the one he's  talking about where he says Kang has  dominion over time he's a time traveler  but then he is actually talking about a  different one where he says his  situation is a little bit different in  this movie that is because as we know  from the trailers one variant of King is  stuck stuck inside of the quantum realm  and he needs Ant-Man to steal something  for him to get out we've seen this power  source in the trailer before and this is  most likely what king the Conqueror  needs to power his time chair his time  chair in the comics is pretty simple  it's how he travels through time we get  a little glimpse of this in the Ant-Man  and the WASP quantumania trailer but we  also get a glimpse at the other Kang the  king that is essentially in charge of  the quantum realm we see the huge  Quantum City we see the huge Army that  King the Conqueror has we see all of the  advanced technology and we see what  seemed to be different portals going out  of the quantum realm these are what Kang  the one in charge most likely uses to  travel through different points in the  universe and not just our universe but  of course the Multiverse so there's  going to be a main Kang and then the  King on the sidelines asking Ant-Man for  help so essentially Ant-Man is already  going after the big bad that literally  The Avengers are going to go after in  the King Dynasty and then the  multiversal heroes are then going to go  after in secret Wars so in this film  it's up to our tiny little Ant-Man  family to take on probably the biggest  and baddest villain that we've ever seen  in the MCU so far and hopefully we get a  better look at Kang in the next trailer  that has come we're actually getting a  special clip trailer Monday the 9th this  will be on ESPN and Marvel has already  marketed this as a new exclusive look  trailer like I said it's debuting on  ESPN at some point in time during the  national college football championship  game that's going to start at 7 30  Eastern time if you need to convert that  into your own time just type it into  Google and of course it's going to be  put on YouTube probably exactly at the  same time as it releases that's what  Marvel Studios has typically been doing  so Ant-Man 3 is going to be a huge movie  on the same level as an Avengers movie  which is just awesome it's about time  that Ant-Man and the wasp and the rest  of the family are getting the credit and  attention that they deserve and to top  it all off like I mentioned in the  beginning we do have some news about  Jessica Jones possibly returning to the  MCU now we've been hearing rumors about  this possibly happening for some time  now we've even gotten some reports from  some insiders and since Charlie Cox has  returned as Daredevil we now know that  it is actually possible for some of  these Defenders from the Netflix series  to return and now actress Kristen Ritter  who of course plays Jessica Jones  herself has posted some pictures to  Instagram of her training with a  daredevil shirt on this is very  interesting as I'm sure most Marvel  actors know what they're doing when they  share photos like this wearing that type  of shirt it's also very interesting to  note that Daredevil born again which she  is rumored to appear in starts filming  next month so is she training for a  cameo and Daredevil born again right now  or possibly another project such as the  echo series which Daredevil is confirmed  to be in as well the timing certainly is  very coincidental probably a little bit  more than coincidental since Charlie Cox  has returned as Daredevil D'Onofrio has  returned as Kingpin I'm assuming that  we're going to see cameos from these  other characters as well perhaps not all  of them but I would love to see Jessica  Jones return which it kind of does look  like is going to happen and I would love  to see of course Frank Castle The  Punisher of course played by John  Bernthal I don't want it unless he is  going to be playing him but it looks  like there are some very exciting things  coming up in the MCU for those who  thought phase 4 might have been a little  bit Bland the future of Phase 5 and  phase six is looking very very good and  even Beyond because we know that the  X-Men and the Fantastic Four are going  to be really big focuses of phase seven  eight and beyond that as well so drop  some comments down below about how  excited you are for Ant-Man and the WASP  Quantum Mania the possibility of Jessica  Jones returning to the MCU or I should  say making her debut in the MCU and of  course Phase 5 and phase six altogether  don't forget to like the video and  subscribe to stay up to date on all the  latest MCU news and you can follow us on  Instagram and Twitter as well as always  thank you all so much for watching wolf  wolf
 

